"""
Natural-convection film coefficient on a room-side wall, floor or ceiling surface.

Ported from `ShipSIM.Components.Others.HeatTransfer.ConvectionFactors.InternalConvection`.
The building-services simplification of natural convection on an internal surface:

```math
h_i = K \\, |\\Delta T|^{1/3}
```

with `K` depending on the surface orientation and on which way the heat flows, because a
horizontal surface either drives a plume or suppresses one:

| `wall_type` | surface colder than air | surface warmer than air |
|---|---|---|
| `Floor` | 0.76 (stable, stratified) | 1.51 (plume rises off the floor) |
| `Ceil` | 1.51 (cold ceiling sheds a plume) | 0.76 (stable) |
| `Wall` | 1.3 | 1.3 |

The orientation is a `structural parameter`, so it is fixed per instance and the two
horizontal cases cost nothing at run time; only the direction of the heat flow is
switched continuously.

Deviation from upstream, numerical: upstream writes `hi = 0` for `|ΔT| <= eps` and
`hi = K·|ΔT|^(1/3)` otherwise, and its own source comments that "this equation produces
initialization failures" — the cube root has an infinite derivative at `ΔT = 0`, which is
exactly where a thermal model is usually initialized. This port uses the smooth

```math
h_i = K \\left(\\Delta T^2 + \\delta^2\\right)^{1/6}
```

which matches `K·|ΔT|^(1/3)` to within a part in `(δ/ΔT)²` once `|ΔT| >> δ`, has a bounded
derivative everywhere, and tends to `K·δ^(1/3)` rather than 0 at equal temperatures.

`δ` defaults to 0.1 K, which puts that floor at about 0.6 W/(m²·K). Smaller values are
not more accurate, only more brittle: a tenth of a kelvin across a bulkhead is below what
the correlation resolves, and driving the floor to zero leaves the surface effectively
insulated from the air at the moment a model is usually initialised — which is what makes
a compartment's initialisation solve fail to converge.
"""
enum WallType =
  | Floor
  | Ceil
  | Wall

component InternalConvection
  extends ConvectionBaseClass
  "Wall surface area [m²]"
  parameter Surf::Area
  "Surface orientation (Floor | Ceil | Wall)"
  structural parameter wall_type::WallType = WallType.Wall()
  "Temperature-difference scale below which the cube root is rounded off [K]"
  parameter dT_eps::Real = 0.1

  "Orientation and flow-direction coefficient [W/(m²·K^(4/3))]"
  variable K::Real
relations
  A = Surf

  switch wall_type
  case Floor
    K = ifelse(ΔT <= 0, 0.76, 1.51)
  case Ceil
    K = ifelse(ΔT <= 0, 1.51, 0.76)
  case Wall
    K = 1.3
  end

  h = K * (ΔT ^ 2 + dT_eps ^ 2) ^ (1 / 6)
end
